        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{1}{2^{\\frac{1}{20}}}$\n\nAdd the indices, then write the negative power as a reciprocal.",
          "worked": "$\\begin{align*}2^{\\frac{1}{5}}\\times2^{-\\frac{1}{4}}&=2^{\\frac{1}{5}-\\frac{1}{4}}\\\\2^{\\frac{1}{5}}\\times2^{-\\frac{1}{4}}&=2^{\\frac{4}{20}-\\frac{5}{20}}\\\\2^{\\frac{1}{5}}\\times2^{-\\frac{1}{4}}&=2^{-\\frac{1}{20}}\\\\2^{\\frac{1}{5}}\\times2^{-\\frac{1}{4}}&=\\frac{1}{2^{\\frac{1}{20}}}\\end{align*}$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
